{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://agentlock.dev/schema/v1.4",
  "title": "AgentLock Tool Definition Schema v1.4",
  "description": "Authorization schema for AI agent tool calls. Defines the agentlock permissions block that extends standard tool definitions with access control, rate limiting, data policies, audit requirements, adaptive hardening, DEFER/STEP_UP/MODIFY decision types, signed receipts, hash-chained context, provenance-lineage gating (session write-gate, parameter lineage, and novel lineage), and selective action-class gating (deletion, membership change, value-carrying).",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "name": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Tool identifier"
    },
    "description": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Human-readable tool description"
    },
    "parameters": {
      "type": "object",
      "description": "Tool parameter schema"
    },
    "agentlock": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/AgentLockPermissions"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "name",
    "agentlock"
  ],
  "$defs": {
    "ActionClassConfig": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Declares a tool's action class in the trusted permission block (v1.4).\n\nSelective action-class gating expands the *trusted-assertion surface*.\nUnder a uniform write-gate, the ``is_*`` flags a caller passes to\n``authorize()`` are safe to get wrong at the sub-class level: any\nconsequential write is gated regardless.  Once ``gate_consequential`` can\nbe turned off independently of ``gate_deletion`` /\n``gate_membership_change``, a caller that simply *omits* ``is_deletion``\nwould slip a deletion past the taint gate.  The action class therefore\nlives here \u2014 registered with the tool, on the trusted side \u2014 rather than\nonly in the per-call, caller-asserted kwarg.\n\nResolution is **monotone OR**: the effective class is\n``declared or caller_asserted``.  A declaration can only ever *add*\ngating.  A tool declared ``is_deletion=True`` cannot be escaped by\nomitting the kwarg, and an absent (or False) declaration can never cancel\na class the caller did assert.  There is deliberately no way to use this\nblock to switch a class *off*; ``gate_*`` on ``LineagePolicyConfig`` is\nthe knob for that, and it lives in trusted config too.\n\nTHE POLARITY RULE \u2014 the invariant future contributors must not break:\n\n* **Gating-ADDING** signals (``is_deletion``, ``is_membership_change``)\n  may originate from the trusted block OR the caller's ``authorize()``\n  kwarg, and combine by OR.  A wrong or missing one can only under-gate\n  the tool relative to a correct one, and the caller can always add.\n* **Gating-REMOVING** signals (``is_value_carrying``) may originate\n  **ONLY** from the trusted block \u2014 never a caller kwarg \u2014 and may weaken\n  **ONLY** the residual ``is_consequential`` disjunct, never a named\n  class.  Admitting a removing signal from the caller, or letting one\n  reach the deletion / membership terms, reintroduces exactly the bypass\n  this design closes.\n\nClassify every future action class into one polarity before adding it.\n\n``is_value_carrying`` is a positive, trusted, auditable claim that this\ntool's consequential effect is fully determined by an attacker-choosable\nparameter value \u2014 so parameter/novel lineage already covers it and\nsession taint need not.  It exists because ``is_consequential`` is not a\nclass but the *residual bucket* (\"consequential, but none of the named\nclasses\"), which makes ``gate_consequential=False`` un-gate an open-ended\nset: every consequential tool nobody got around to classifying.  Requiring\na positive declaration to un-gate means an unclassified consequential\naction fails CLOSED (stays gated, costing recoverable utility) rather\nthan OPEN (a silent hole on precisely the value-free classes for which\nsession taint is the only available signal).\n\nUn-gating therefore takes two affirmative acts: the deployment sets\n``gate_consequential=False``, and the tool declares\n``is_value_carrying=True``.  Omitting either leaves the action gated.",
      "properties": {
        "is_deletion": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Is Deletion",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "is_membership_change": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Is Membership Change",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "is_value_carrying": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Is Value Carrying",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "title": "ActionClassConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "AgentLockPermissions": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "The ``agentlock`` permissions block attached to a tool definition.\n\nThis is the core of the specification.  Every field has a secure default\nso that an empty permissions block denies by default.\n\nExample::\n\n    perms = AgentLockPermissions(\n        risk_level=\"high\",\n        requires_auth=True,\n        allowed_roles=[\"admin\"],\n    )",
      "properties": {
        "version": {
          "default": "1.4",
          "title": "Version",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "risk_level": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/RiskLevel",
          "default": "high"
        },
        "requires_auth": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Requires Auth",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "auth_methods": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/AuthMethod"
          },
          "title": "Auth Methods",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "allowed_roles": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Allowed Roles",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "scope": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ScopeConfig"
        },
        "rate_limit": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/RateLimitConfig"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "data_policy": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/DataPolicyConfig"
        },
        "session": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/SessionConfig"
        },
        "audit": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/AuditConfig"
        },
        "human_approval": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/HumanApprovalConfig"
        },
        "context_policy": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/ContextPolicyConfig"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "memory_policy": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/MemoryPolicyConfig"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "modify_policy": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/ModifyPolicyConfig"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "defer_policy": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/DeferPolicyConfig"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "stepup_policy": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/StepUpPolicyConfig"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "lineage_policy": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/LineagePolicyConfig"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "action_class": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/ActionClassConfig"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        }
      },
      "title": "AgentLockPermissions",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ApprovalChannel": {
      "description": "Out-of-band approval delivery channel.",
      "enum": [
        "push_notification",
        "email",
        "sms",
        "in_app"
      ],
      "title": "ApprovalChannel",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "ApprovalThreshold": {
      "description": "When human approval is triggered.",
      "enum": [
        "always",
        "bulk_operations",
        "external_communication",
        "financial_above_limit",
        "first_invocation_per_session"
      ],
      "title": "ApprovalThreshold",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "AuditConfig": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Audit logging requirements.  Audit is never optional.",
      "properties": {
        "log_level": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/AuditLogLevel",
          "default": "standard"
        },
        "include_parameters": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Include Parameters",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "retention_days": {
          "default": 90,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Retention Days",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "title": "AuditConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "AuditLogLevel": {
      "description": "Audit detail level.",
      "enum": [
        "minimal",
        "standard",
        "full"
      ],
      "title": "AuditLogLevel",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "AuthMethod": {
      "description": "Supported authentication mechanisms.",
      "enum": [
        "oauth2",
        "magic_link",
        "mfa",
        "api_key"
      ],
      "title": "AuthMethod",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "ContextAuthority": {
      "description": "Trust level of a context source.",
      "enum": [
        "authoritative",
        "derived",
        "untrusted"
      ],
      "title": "ContextAuthority",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "ContextPolicyConfig": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Governs what enters context and with what authority.",
      "properties": {
        "source_authorities": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/SourceAuthorityConfig"
          },
          "title": "Source Authorities",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "trust_degradation": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/TrustDegradationConfig"
        },
        "reject_unattributed": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Reject Unattributed",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "title": "ContextPolicyConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ContextSource": {
      "description": "Sources of context entries in the agent's context window.",
      "enum": [
        "user_message",
        "system_prompt",
        "tool_output",
        "retrieved_document",
        "web_content",
        "agent_memory",
        "peer_agent"
      ],
      "title": "ContextSource",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "DataBoundary": {
      "description": "Scope of data access.",
      "enum": [
        "authenticated_user_only",
        "team",
        "organization"
      ],
      "title": "DataBoundary",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "DataClassification": {
      "description": "Data sensitivity classification.",
      "enum": [
        "public",
        "internal",
        "confidential",
        "may_contain_pii",
        "contains_pii",
        "contains_phi",
        "contains_financial"
      ],
      "title": "DataClassification",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "DataPolicyConfig": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Data classification and redaction rules.",
      "properties": {
        "input_classification": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/DataClassification",
          "default": "public"
        },
        "output_classification": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/DataClassification",
          "default": "public"
        },
        "prohibited_in_output": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Prohibited In Output",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "redaction": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/RedactionMode",
          "default": "none"
        }
      },
      "title": "DataPolicyConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "DeferPolicyConfig": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Governs when authorization is suspended pending resolution (v1.2).\n\nDEFER acknowledges uncertainty: the gate cannot confidently allow or\ndeny.  The action is suspended until resolved by human review,\nadditional context, or timeout.",
      "properties": {
        "enabled": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Enabled",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "first_call_any_risk": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "First Call Any Risk",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "first_call_high_risk": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "First Call High Risk",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "scan_plus_tool": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Scan Plus Tool",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "trust_below_threshold": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Trust Below Threshold",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "timeout_seconds": {
          "default": 60,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Timeout Seconds",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "timeout_action": {
          "default": "deny",
          "title": "Timeout Action",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "title": "DeferPolicyConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "DegradationEffect": {
      "description": "Effect applied when trust degrades.",
      "enum": [
        "require_approval",
        "elevate_logging",
        "restrict_scope",
        "deny_writes"
      ],
      "title": "DegradationEffect",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "DegradationTrigger": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Defines when and how trust degrades.",
      "properties": {
        "source": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ContextSource"
        },
        "effect": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/DegradationEffect"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "source",
        "effect"
      ],
      "title": "DegradationTrigger",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "HumanApprovalConfig": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Human-in-the-loop approval gate.",
      "properties": {
        "required": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Required",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "threshold": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ApprovalThreshold",
          "default": "always"
        },
        "channel": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ApprovalChannel",
          "default": "push_notification"
        }
      },
      "title": "HumanApprovalConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "LineagePolicyConfig": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Governs provenance-lineage gating of tool calls (v1.3).\n\nA tool is gated purely on the *provenance* of what is already in the\nsession's context window \u2014 not on the content of its parameters.  If\nuntrusted content (authority ``UNTRUSTED``) has entered context, a\ngated action (financial / external / bulk) is blocked.  This is the\nopposite of a content rule: it never inspects the payload, only where\nthe session's context came from.\n\nWhen ``require_post_authoritative`` is True, only untrusted content\nthat entered *after* the last authoritative (user/system) message\ntaints the action \u2014 an untrusted document read before the user's\ninstruction does not, but one read after it does.",
      "properties": {
        "enabled": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Enabled",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "gate_financial": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Gate Financial",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "gate_external": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Gate External",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "gate_bulk": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Gate Bulk",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "gate_account_modification": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Gate Account Modification",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "gate_consequential": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Gate Consequential",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "gate_deletion": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Gate Deletion",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "gate_membership_change": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Gate Membership Change",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "decision": {
          "default": "step_up",
          "title": "Decision",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "require_post_authoritative": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Require Post Authoritative",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "session_write_gate": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Session Write Gate",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "param_lineage_enabled": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Param Lineage Enabled",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "param_lineage_action": {
          "default": "deny",
          "title": "Param Lineage Action",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "param_lineage_min_len": {
          "default": 6,
          "title": "Param Lineage Min Len",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "novel_lineage_enabled": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Novel Lineage Enabled",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "novel_lineage_action": {
          "default": "step_up",
          "title": "Novel Lineage Action",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "title": "LineagePolicyConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "MemoryPersistence": {
      "description": "Memory persistence scope.",
      "enum": [
        "none",
        "session",
        "cross_session"
      ],
      "title": "MemoryPersistence",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "MemoryPolicyConfig": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Governs what the agent can persist to memory.",
      "properties": {
        "persistence": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/MemoryPersistence",
          "default": "none"
        },
        "allowed_writers": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/MemoryWriter"
          },
          "title": "Allowed Writers",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "allowed_readers": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/MemoryWriter"
          },
          "title": "Allowed Readers",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "retention": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/MemoryRetentionConfig"
        },
        "prohibited_content": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Prohibited Content",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "require_write_confirmation": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Require Write Confirmation",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "confirmation_channel": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ApprovalChannel",
          "default": "in_app"
        }
      },
      "title": "MemoryPolicyConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "MemoryRetentionConfig": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Retention limits for persistent memory.",
      "properties": {
        "max_age_seconds": {
          "default": 86400,
          "minimum": 0,
          "title": "Max Age Seconds",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "max_entries": {
          "default": 100,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Max Entries",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "title": "MemoryRetentionConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "MemoryWriter": {
      "description": "Entities that can write to or read from agent memory.",
      "enum": [
        "system",
        "user",
        "agent",
        "tool"
      ],
      "title": "MemoryWriter",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "ModifyPolicyConfig": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Governs parameter and output transformations (v1.2).\n\nWhen enabled, the gate applies transformations to tool parameters\nor outputs before/after execution.  The tool still runs, but its\ninputs or outputs are sanitized.",
      "properties": {
        "enabled": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Enabled",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "transformations": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/TransformationConfig"
          },
          "title": "Transformations",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "apply_when_hardening_active": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Apply When Hardening Active",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "title": "ModifyPolicyConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "RateLimitConfig": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Per-user, per-session rate limiting.",
      "properties": {
        "max_calls": {
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Max Calls",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "window_seconds": {
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Window Seconds",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "max_calls",
        "window_seconds"
      ],
      "title": "RateLimitConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "RecipientPolicy": {
      "description": "Allowed recipient scope for outbound communication tools.",
      "enum": [
        "known_contacts_only",
        "same_domain",
        "allowlist",
        "any"
      ],
      "title": "RecipientPolicy",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "RedactionMode": {
      "description": "How prohibited data types are handled.",
      "enum": [
        "auto",
        "manual",
        "none"
      ],
      "title": "RedactionMode",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "RiskLevel": {
      "description": "Tool risk classification.",
      "enum": [
        "none",
        "low",
        "medium",
        "high",
        "critical"
      ],
      "title": "RiskLevel",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "ScopeConfig": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Constrains what data a tool invocation can access.",
      "properties": {
        "data_boundary": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/DataBoundary",
          "default": "authenticated_user_only"
        },
        "max_records": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "minimum": 1,
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Max Records"
        },
        "allowed_recipients": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/RecipientPolicy",
          "default": "known_contacts_only"
        }
      },
      "title": "ScopeConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "SessionConfig": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Session lifetime and re-authentication rules.",
      "properties": {
        "max_duration_seconds": {
          "default": 900,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Max Duration Seconds",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "require_reauth_on_scope_change": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Require Reauth On Scope Change",
          "type": "boolean"
        }
      },
      "title": "SessionConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "SourceAuthorityConfig": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Maps a context source to an authority level.",
      "properties": {
        "source": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ContextSource"
        },
        "authority": {
          "$ref": "#/$defs/ContextAuthority"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "source",
        "authority"
      ],
      "title": "SourceAuthorityConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "StepUpPolicyConfig": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Governs when human approval is dynamically required (v1.2).\n\nSTEP_UP pauses execution and notifies a human reviewer.  Unlike the\nstatic ``human_approval`` config, STEP_UP is triggered by session\nstate (hardening signals, PII tool count, prior denials).",
      "properties": {
        "enabled": {
          "default": false,
          "title": "Enabled",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "hardening_elevated_high_risk": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Hardening Elevated High Risk",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "multi_pii_tool_session": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Multi Pii Tool Session",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "multi_pii_tool_threshold": {
          "default": 2,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Multi Pii Tool Threshold",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "post_denial_retry": {
          "default": true,
          "title": "Post Denial Retry",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "timeout_seconds": {
          "default": 120,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Timeout Seconds",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "timeout_action": {
          "default": "deny",
          "title": "Timeout Action",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "pii_tool_names": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Pii Tool Names",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "title": "StepUpPolicyConfig",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "TransformationConfig": {
